course: dictionary
lesson: 12578
title: Dimmed: less bright, or less strong
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Dimmed means made less bright, or became less bright. Look at the words around it to find the meaning. «The lights dimmed slowly as the film began.» The clues are film began and slowly. The lights did not go out; they got less bright. Try your meaning in the sentence: the lights got less bright as the film began. That makes sense, so dimmed means made less bright.
explain: Dimmed can also describe feelings and hopes. «Bad news dimmed her hopes of winning.» Her hopes did not vanish in a flash. They became weaker, like a light going dim. So dimmed can mean a feeling or hope became weaker.
explain: Drivers use dimmed too. «Dad dimmed the headlights so the driver coming towards us was not dazzled.» Dimmed headlights point lower, so they do not dazzle other drivers. The word dim is the base: dim, dims, dimmed, dimming.
fact: Dim means less bright. Dimmed is the past form of dim.
fact: «The lights dimmed» means the lights were made less bright, or became less bright.
fact: «Dimmed hopes» means hopes that have become weaker.
fact: On a car, «dimmed» headlights point lower so they do not dazzle other drivers.
fact: A dimmed lamp gives out less light energy.
exercise: «The lights dimmed as the film began.» What does dimmed mean here? | Made louder | Switched on for the first time | Turned into a rainbow | *Made less bright
exercise: «Bad news dimmed her hopes of winning.» Which word is closest in meaning to dimmed? | Doubled | Shouted | *Weakened | Painted
exercise: «Dad dimmed the headlights so the driver coming towards us was not dazzled.» Why did Dad do this? | *To stop dazzling other drivers | To make the car go faster | To find his keys in the dark | To wake the dog
test: «The room dimmed when the storm clouds covered the sun.» Find and copy one word that means made less bright. | room | storm | *dimmed | sun
test: «Hope dimmed in his heart after the letter came.» What does dimmed mean here? | Became louder | *Became weaker | Grew taller | Became wet
exam: Which sentence uses dimmed to mean made weaker? | «The lamp dimmed in the corner.» | «The car dimmed its lights at night.» | «The room dimmed when the power cut out.» | *«Bad news dimmed his hopes.»
